name=GoM Extension: Guns of Tien
id=GoMExtensionGunsOfTien
description=More ammunition for Guns of Marz, all real loads of 1993: subsonic, hollow point, soft point, steel core, +P and +P+ rounds, birdshot, the new .22 LR calibre with subsonic, hollow point and hyper velocity loads, and the AS VAL's SP-6. Adjusted gun sounds, full metal jacket rifle rounds pierce, the break-action shotguns' stocks can be sawn off to fit a holster, the Mosin-Nagant can be sawn into an Obrez, an AWC Mk9 suppressor, every 9mm suppressor fitting every 9mm pistol and submachine gun, Guns of Marz's MP5 shown as the MP5A3, the Uzi, Mini Uzi and Micro Uzi, the Steyr TMP machine pistol, the Steyr AUG A1 with its integral scope and folding front grip, the Glock 21, the Walther PPK in .22 LR (fits an ankle holster), the SR-25 match rifle with its built-in scope and folding bipod, the FN P90 with its ring sight and 5.7x28mm SS190 rounds, the M249 light machine gun, the RPK and RPK-74 with their folding bipods and the RPK's 40-round magazine and 75-round drum (both also fit Guns of Marz's AK-47), the RPD with its 100-round belt drum, the SVU bullpup Dragunov with folding sights, Guns of Marz's Picatinny rails fitting the AUG A1, Uzi, Mini Uzi, P90 and M249; guns held like a pistol hang upright on other mods' attachment slots; belt-fed guns (the M249 and the M60) now need belt links, found or made (can be switched off); a shot hitting several targets can roll its critical hits per target again, as before Build 42.22, and a gun's failed hit roll on a zombie can still do a share of its damage (sandbox options). Every gun's tooltip is written from what it really takes, every 9mm gun shares one muzzle mount, every gun takes its calibre's muzzle mount where its muzzle parts fit (suppressors only where the real gun takes one), real flash hiders, compensators and muzzle brakes (the AKM slant compensator, AK-74 brake, AKS-74U booster, MP5 flash hider, Clark race compensators, the Thompson's Cutts), and guns saved with a part they no longer take have it taken off and put beside them (sandbox option). A fitted bayonet can be put to use with its own key (or the radial or gun menu): the gun becomes a spear that trains Spear until put back (sandbox option, off by default). With Ammo Maker, every new round can be made, and its part boxes can be packed into cartons and crates (sandbox option). Needs Gunworks-gang and Guns of Marz. Follows Guns of Marz's November 2026 update: each gun's optimal range by its class, flat attachment bonuses, one shot per click on semi-automatic and bolt guns, suppressors that wear (shown on the gun's tooltip) and are repaired, broken ones too, tool-free attachments once their mount is on, found suppressors and muzzle devices with their mount, Guns of Marz's SMG and foregrip stances on the two-handed submachine guns and bullpups, Gunworks' Swap for the folding front grips, and both sides of the jungle-taped STANAG pair. Every gun is held and reloaded with Guns of Marz's own animations, its bolt moving in the ejection port on each shot and its charging handle only when racked, as on the real guns.
